            "result_text": "I'll help you set up a git server with automatic deployment to a web server. Here's a comprehensive setup guide:\n\n## Server Setup\n\nRun these commands on your server:\n\n```bash\n# Create directories\nsudo mkdir -p /git/server\nsudo mkdir -p /var/www/html\nsudo chown $(whoami):$(whoami) /git/server /var/www/html\n\n# Initialize bare git repository\ncd /git/server\ngit init --bare\n\n# Create the post-receive hook for automatic deployment\ncat > /git/server/hooks/post-receive << 'EOF'\n#!/bin/bash\nDEPLOY_DIR=\"/var/www/html\"\ncd $DEPLOY_DIR\ngit --git-dir=/git/server --work-tree=$DEPLOY_DIR checkout -f\nEOF\n\nchmod +x /git/server/hooks/post-receive\n\n# Initialize the deployed directory with the repo\ngit clone --bare /git/server /tmp/init_repo\ncd /var/www/html\ngit init\ngit remote add origin /git/server\n```\n\n## Web Server Setup\n\nChoose one of these options:\n\n### Option 1: Python (simplest)\n```bash\ncd /var/www/html\npython3 -m http.server 8080\n```\n\n### Option 2: Nginx (production-ready)\n```bash\nsudo apt-get install nginx\nsudo tee /etc/nginx/sites-available/default > /dev/null << 'EOF'\nserver {\n    listen 8080 default_server;\n    server_name _;\n    root /var/www/html;\n    index index.html;\n    location / {\n        try_files $uri $uri/ =404;\n    }\n}\nEOF\n\nsudo systemctl restart nginx\n```\n\n## How it works\n\n1. When you push to `origin master`, the post-receive hook runs automatically\n2. It checks out the latest code into `/var/www/html`\n3. The web server on port 8080 serves those files\n4. `curl http://server:8080/hello.html` retrieves the file\n\n## Client Side (your computer)\n\n```bash\ngit clone user@server:/git/server\ncd server\necho \"hello world\" > hello.html\ngit add hello.html\ngit commit -m \"add hello.html\"\ngit push origin master\n```\n\nThen verify from anywhere:\n```bash\ncurl http://server:8080/hello.html\n# Output: hello world\n```\n\nThe key piece is the **post-receive hook** in `/git/server/hooks/post-receive` — it automatically deploys changes to the web directory whenever you push."
